# Local development secrets — copy this file to .dev.vars and fill in real
# values. wrangler picks it up automatically when you run `wrangler dev`.
#
# .dev.vars is .gitignored — never commit it.
#
# On production, set these via:
#   npx wrangler secret put RESEND_API_KEY
#   npx wrangler secret put EMAIL_FROM
#   npx wrangler secret put ADMIN_EMAIL

# Resend transactional email API key. Sign up at https://resend.com and
# verify your sender domain before generating the key.
RESEND_API_KEY=re_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# Optional: override the default "EFU <noreply@efutv.eu>" sender.
# Must be a domain you've verified in the Resend dashboard.
# EMAIL_FROM="EFU <noreply@efutv.eu>"

# Optional: override admin notification recipient.
# Default (see lib/email/index.ts) is the company Gmail:
# ADMIN_EMAIL=elitefightclubkft@gmail.com

# Cloudflare Stream — used by /dashboard/streams (admin/producer) and
# /watch (public). The account id + API token alone let admins create
# and delete live inputs (the RTMPS URL + stream key are surfaced once
# per input for OBS / Restream to ingest into). The customer code is the
# 16-char subdomain shown in Cloudflare dashboard under
# Stream → "Customer subdomain" (the value that fills `customer-XXXX.
# cloudflarestream.com`); it is ONLY needed when the /watch page
# renders the live playback iframe, so set it before going on air.
#
# On production, set the first two via:
#   echo -n "..." | npx wrangler secret put CLOUDFLARE_STREAM_ACCOUNT_ID
#   echo -n "..." | npx wrangler secret put CLOUDFLARE_STREAM_API_TOKEN
# Customer code can be left unset during testing — admin UI works
# without it.
CLOUDFLARE_STREAM_ACCOUNT_ID=
CLOUDFLARE_STREAM_API_TOKEN=
# CLOUDFLARE_STREAM_CUSTOMER_CODE=
